{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_uwm4xcg5md6dcrxe65whjjllbkvsm45drxaqzzuvofud4oapoodq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. **Exit 0 across the full matrix; the Rust translation required no fixes.**\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src` is a single 21-line translation unit with one exported function:\n`int wcscat(wchar_t *dst, size_t numElem, const wchar_t *src)` — a bounded\n`wcscat_s`-style append returning `0` / `22` (EINVAL) / `34` (ERANGE).\n\n## Phase A — artifacts (crate root)\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` for both `.so`s. C exports exactly `wcscat`; Rust exports `wcscat`. **Symbol diff = empty.** No C module was left untranslated (only `lib.c` exists), so no new translation was needed. Also records the verified ABI facts: `sizeof(wchar_t)==4`, signed, C built at `-O0 -fPIC`. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 18 rows, derived by inventorying every `return 22`/`return 34`/guard in `lib.c` (no asserts/enums/NULL-returns exist), plus 5 generic FFI-boundary rows. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 10 branch axes extracted from the source, pruned to 28 distinct valid-path combinations (NUL position `k`, fit class, `numElem` classes incl. wrap-around, payload value classes, aliasing, window-vs-allocation, repeated calls). |\n\nFeature combinations: Cargo.toml had no `[features]`; the C build has no `option()`/`-D`/`#ifdef`. I added `default = []` and enumerated the complete set — `<none>`, `default`, implicit-default — all checked/built/tested.\n\n## A critical harness bug I found and fixed\n\n`cargo test` does **not** rebuild a `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`-only library (integration tests can't link it, so it isn't a dependency of the test target). My first harness loaded `target/debug/libwcscat_lib.so` directly and **passed all 28 tests against deliberately broken Rust**. I proved this by injecting `34 → 35` and an off-by-one loop bound: both went undetected.\n\n`tests/common/mod.rs` now builds the cdylib itself into `target/difftest/<features>/` with the same feature set as the running test binary. After the fix, a 7-mutation battery (`22→23`, `34→35`, `0→1`, dropped `numElem==0` guard, dropped either `dst[0]=0` store, reordered `!dst`/`!src` guards, loop-bound off-by-ones) each made the suite fail; reverting restored green.\n\n## Phases B–D — results\n\n- **Phase B:** 28/28 `CONFIGS.md` rows, each with 100–2400 randomized inputs (fixed-seed SplitMix64). Comparison is byte-for-byte over the *whole* allocation plus the `src` buffer, so partial-copy-then-`dst[0]=0` behaviour and write extents are pinned exactly.\n- **Phase C:** 23/23 rows. Every test asserts the exact code (`22`/`34`/`0`) and exact memory image — including the subtle `numElem==0` short-circuit that must *not* clear `dst[0]`, the `!src` branch winning over `SIZE_MAX`, and the pointer-arithmetic wrap boundaries (`2^62`, `2^62+1`, `SIZE_MAX`, `2^63`) where `dst + numElem` lands *below* `dst`. For the \"out-of-range enum\" class (this API has no enum) I used the analogue: `wchar_t` values with no valid Unicode meaning (negatives, `INT_MIN/MAX`, lone surrogates, `>0x10FFFF`, `0x80000000`).\n- **Phase D:** `tests/symbols.rs` automates the `nm -D` diff, checks for undefined non-system symbols and leaked Rust internals, and guards against `dlsym` silently resolving either side to glibc's unrelated 2-argument `wcscat`.\n- **All of the above ran under both feature combos × both Rust profiles (debug and release/`panic=\"abort\"`)** — 20 suite runs, 228 test executions, 0 failures. `run_all_features.sh` automates it and exits non-zero on divergence (verified).\n\nNothing in `c_src/` was modified. `src/lib.rs` is byte-identical to the incoming translation — it was already correct, including the wrapping-pointer semantics and the C's quirky truncation stores."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":142914,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1531,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":142914},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"665ffee4-01f9-4fcf-be0a-78d2d67f6671","uuid":"c12a8c3b-5b63-4290-9be3-13c9ff1639cd","timestamp":"2026-08-19T15:58:08.609Z"}
